Overview [#over]
****************

The Pyschrometrics extension provides a set of functions for basic
[psychrometric]`http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychrometrics` and related
calculations implemented in Axon. Credit goes to Eric Kozubal for providing the
Microsoft Excel VBA macros originally used to create this extension.

For a change log, see the
[psychrometricsExt]`https://github.com/NatLabRockies/psychrometricsExt`
repository on GitHub.

Usage Notes
===========

- The `psychSolver()` function is a flexible "one stop shop" for calculating
  most pyschrometric properties supported by this extension. (Thank you to
  James Donson for contributing the initial implementation of this function!)
- Other functions calculate various properties of dry air, moist air, liquid
  water, and glycol-water mixtures. The functions are individually documented.
- Some function families support calculating the same output value given
  different input states. For example, the functions `relativeHumidity()`,
  `relativeHumidity2()`, and `relativeHumidity3()` all calculate relative
  humidity but differ in their required inputs.
  
Units
=====

- Function inputs may be in any valid units for the input quantity (as defined
  by the Haystack units database). Inputs are converted to standard SI units
  within each function.
- With the exception of `psychSolver()`, function outputs are always in standard
  SI units. (`psychSolver()` allows the user to specify either SI or IP units
  via the 'outputUnits' option.)